<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cen Yuying</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829–1889</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cen Yuying was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> official from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a> who rose to prominence suppressing the Panthay Rebellion of the Hui Muslims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>. As governor of Yunnan he led the campaign that besieged and took Dali in 1872–1873, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/du-wenxiu">Du Wenxiu</a>'s state. He later served as governor-general of Yunnan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guizhou">Guizhou</a> and directed Qing forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-french-war">Sino-French War</a> of 1884–1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cen-yuying.jpg" alt="Cen Yuying" width="300" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (Qing)Zhao Fan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_portrait_of_Cen_Yuying.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
